{"corpus":"ccc","number":500,"text_html":"<span>À cela on objecte parfois que l’Écriture mentionne des frères et sœurs de Jésus <sup class=\"srcRef bibleRef\" data-idx=\"1\">1</sup>. L’Église a toujours compris ces passages comme ne désignant pas d’autres enfants de la Vierge Marie : en effet Jacques et Joseph, « frères de Jésus » <sup class=\"srcRef bibleRef\" data-idx=\"5\">2</sup>, sont les fils d’une Marie disciple du Christ <sup class=\"srcRef bibleRef\" data-idx=\"6\">3</sup> qui est désignée de manière significative comme « l’autre Marie » <sup class=\"srcRef bibleRef\" data-idx=\"7\">4</sup>. Il s’agit de proches parents de Jésus, selon une expression connue de l’Ancien Testament <sup class=\"srcRef bibleRef\" data-idx=\"8\">5</sup>.</span>","cross_refs":[],"bible_refs":[{"text":"Mc 3:31-35"},{"text":"Mc 6:3"},{"text":"1 Co 9:5"},{"text":"Ga 1:19"},{"text":"Mt 13:55"},{"text":"Mt 27:56"},{"text":"Mt 28:1"},{"text":"Gn 13:8"},{"text":"Gn 14:16"},{"text":"Gn 29:15"}],"citations":[],"magisterial_refs":[{"type":"bible","raw":"voir Mc 3:31-35","idx":1,"display_idx":1},{"type":"bible_continuation","raw":"6:3","idx":2,"marker_idx":1,"display_idx":1},{"type":"bible","raw":"1 Co 9:5","idx":3,"marker_idx":1,"display_idx":1},{"type":"bible","raw":"Ga 1:19","idx":4,"marker_idx":1,"display_idx":1},{"type":"bible","raw":"Mt 13:55","idx":5,"display_idx":2},{"type":"bible","raw":"voir Mt 27:56","idx":6,"display_idx":3},{"type":"bible","raw":"Mt 28:1","idx":7,"display_idx":4},{"type":"bible","raw":"voir Gn 13:8","idx":8,"display_idx":5},{"type":"bible_continuation","raw":"14:16","idx":9,"marker_idx":8,"display_idx":5},{"type":"bible_continuation","raw":"29:15","idx":10,"marker_idx":8,"display_idx":5}]}